  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine and impacted countries crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response activities (evacuation assistance, mobile heating points).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response activities (evacuation assistance, mobile heating points).
&#x2022; Stabilising access to electricity and heating (through provision of mobile heating boilers, electric 
generators, and &#x201c;no light&#x201d; kits).
&#x2022; Shelter support (reinforced concrete shelters, rehabilitation of critical public infrastructure and 
shelters).
&#x2022; CVA assistance (for home-based care recipients, vulnerable farmers, IDP households and households 
in de-occupied territories), complemented by in-kind relief assistance as required.
&#x2022; Livelihoods support for vulnerable farming communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of the crisis, nearly one third of the total Ukrainians population have been forced from their homes, this marks one of the largest human displacement crises in the world today.
It is estimated that more than 4,1 million people in Ukraine will face extreme winter in 2022-23 and will need external humanitarian assistance</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine and neigbouring countries</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">more than 4,1 million people in Ukraine (and neighbouring countries)</narrative>
  </description>
